From: Jonas Karlsson <jonas.karlsson@qt.io>
Subject: [PATCH] PhysX: Store the padded matrix the way the vecmath in use
 wants

PxMat33Padded picks between V3StoreU() and V4StoreU() from a list of
platforms rather than from the vecmath it is compiled against, and the
list leaves out arm64 macOS: PhysX 5 only turns COMPILE_VECTOR_INTRINSICS
on for the Intel family and for Switch, so every other architecture,
Apple silicon included, gets the scalar vecmath, where Vec3V is a struct
of three floats and V4StoreU() only takes a Vec4V. The store does not
compile there, and it is in a header, so it takes with it every
translation unit that reaches PxSIMDHelpers.h, which CmScaling.h includes
for all of geomutils.

Ask COMPILE_VECTOR_INTRINSICS, which is what decides whether Vec3V and
Vec4V are the same four wide register, instead of naming the platforms
where it happens to be off: that is the condition the two stores actually
differ on. It keeps the two the list did name, PX_SIMD_DISABLED and Linux
on arm, and takes in the ones it did not, arm64 macOS and WebAssembly
with the SIMD extension off.
---
 src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/PxSIMDHelpers.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/PxSIMDHelpers.h b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/PxSIMDHelpers.h
--- a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/PxSIMDHelpers.h
+++ b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/PxSIMDHelpers.h
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@ namespace physx
 			const QuatV qV = V4LoadU(&q.x);
 			Vec3V column0V, column1V, column2V;
 			QuatGetMat33V(qV, column0V, column1V, column2V);
-#if defined(PX_SIMD_DISABLED) || (PX_LINUX && (PX_ARM || PX_A64))
+#if !COMPILE_VECTOR_INTRINSICS
 			V3StoreU(column0V, column0);
 			V3StoreU(column1V, column1);
 			V3StoreU(column2V, column2);
